<TrustPage
  title="Akeru Bot developer guide"
  description="Install the Akeru Bot CLI, learn how it runs locally, and report problems to the maintainers."
  heading="Akeru Bot for developers"
>
  <h2>Akeru Bot CLI</h2>
  <p>
    Akeru Bot is open-source software that runs Grok bots on a user's machine or in a sandbox that
    the user controls. It is an independent alternative to the official Grok Bot product. Install the official
    <a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/akeru-bot">akeru-bot CLI package</a> with
    <code>npx akeru-bot@latest</code>.
    The CLI starts the local server, opens the web client, and manages chats with your bots. The desktop
    app bundles the same server. Source code, releases, user guides, and contribution rules are in
    the <a href="https://github.com/opencoredev/akeru-bot">Akeru Bot GitHub repository</a>.
  </p>
  <h2>No public API on this website</h2>
  <p>
    This website serves static pages and documents only. It has no public API, metadata endpoint, or
    OpenAPI contract, and it never runs a bot or reads user data. Requests under <code>/api</code>
    return an RFC 9457 JSON problem with a stable code and a link back to this guide.
  </p>
  <h2>Akeru Bot local integrations</h2>
  <p>
    Akeru Bot connects to provider CLIs and user-selected tool servers from the local environment.
    It does not provide a hosted automation API or a public MCP server. To configure bot profiles,
    plugins, memory, or remote access, use the
    <a href="https://github.com/opencoredev/akeru-bot/tree/main/docs/user">Akeru Bot user guides</a>.
    Agents should not send project data, credentials, or provider tokens to this marketing domain.
  </p>
  <h2>Send feedback to the Akeru Bot maintainers</h2>
  <p>
    Agents and developers report problems the same way. Read
    <a href="/feedback.md">feedback.md</a> for where a report goes, what to include, and what to
    leave out. A failed command, a wrong page, or docs that do not match the product all belong
    in the <a href="https://github.com/opencoredev/akeru-bot/issues">Akeru Bot issue tracker</a>.
  </p>
</TrustPage>
